{
  "id": "dative-der-words",
  "level": "A2",
  "title": "Wiederholung: Dativ und Der-Wörter",
  "group": "Cases",
  "sourceFile": "dativderwort.html",
  "overview": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": "Der-words carry the same endings as der/die/das. Ein-words carry the same endings as ein/eine. In dative, masculine and neuter end in -em, feminine in -er, and plural in -en."
      },
      {
        "type": "table",
        "content": "",
        "rows": [
          [
            "",
            "Masc.",
            "Fem.",
            "Neut.",
            "Plural"
          ],
          [
            "der-word",
            "diesem",
            "dieser",
            "diesem",
            "diesen"
          ],
          [
            "ein-word",
            "meinem",
            "meiner",
            "meinem",
            "meinen"
          ]
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "content": "Der-words: dieser, jeder, welcher, solcher\nEin-words: ein, kein, mein, dein, sein, ihr, unser, euer, Ihr"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": "Dative plural usually also adds -n to the noun: mit diesen Kindern, von meinen Freunden."
      },
      {
        "type": "example",
        "content": "",
        "de": "Ich kaufe meinem Bruder ein Geschenk.",
        "note": "meinem = dative masculine of mein"
      }
    ]
  },
